BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Energy Science & Engineering] ESE Seminar - Nori Nakata: "Reservo
 ir Evolution and Stress Changes during Enhanced Geothermal System Developm
 ent"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T132000
DTSTAMP:20261026T190345Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54295674034251-54295674036300@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Abstract\n\nUnderstanding reservoir evolution is essential for
  developing enhanced geothermal systems (EGS). Induced seismicity carries 
 rich information about subsurface stress changes and fracture activation d
 uring EGS development. This presentation synthesizes recent studies at Cap
 e Station and Utah FORGE using seismic networks and borehole distributed a
 coustic sensing (DAS). We examine microearthquake stress drops\, image fra
 cture networks through waveform similarity\, and compare focal mechanism\n
 \nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-10-26 12:03 PDT
LOCATION:Green Earth Sciences Building
END:VEVENT
