DTSTAMP:20261026T190345Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54127785305853-54127785306878@local-events
DESCRIPTION:1946. The last French soldier left Syria. A few months before
 \, Tawfiq al-Suweidi\, the Iraqi Prime Minister\, introduced a set of laws
  to protect constitutional freedoms and legalize political parties. In bot
 h post-Ottoman countries\, Iraq and Syria\, the 1940s and 1950s were marke
 d by a contradictory political legacy. On the one hand\, parliaments ruled
 \, political parties flourished\, and civil society gained traction throug
 h public debate. On the other\, emergency laws blocked debate\, or the mil
 itary\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-10-26 12:03 PDT
LOCATION:Encina Commons
END:VEVENT
