 t co-flowing with air streams into a collection of droplets with a wide ra
 nge of applications from industrial to power generation. The application o
 f interest is air-blast atomization\, relevant to fuel injection\, where t
 he co-flowing airstream is at high speeds where compressibility may affect
  atomization. This presentation covers the extension of a high-order compa
 ct finite difference framework to compressible\, two-phase flows for si\n
